  "estbl_tmax": {
   "description": "The upper clamp of the estbl saturation-vapor-pressure lookup: tmax = 375.16 K (wv_saturation.F90:96, the public module parameter; estblf clamps T to it at wv_saturation.F90:388, so the 251st table knot at 377.16 K is unreachable). Zero-parameter constant-fragment template applied with empty bindings.",
   "params": [],
   "body": {
    "op": "const",
    "args": [],
    "value": 375.16,
    "units": "K"
   }
  },
  "estbl_es0": {
   "description": "The saturation vapor pressure of the estbl table lookup, es0 = estbl[min(T, tmax)]: the linear interpolation of the 251-knot estbl function table on the clamped temperature min(T, tmax) (estblf of wv_saturation.F90:388, estbl_tmax the wv_saturation.F90:96 clamp), flat outside the axis. The table data (Goff-Gratch mixed-phase SVP of wv_sat_init, wv_saturation.F90:191-254) now lives IN this template as the esm:std/interp.esm `linear` application's const table (esm 2.0.0 removed function_tables/table_lookup; the 1.x table lowering of esm-spec 1.x §9.5.3 becomes the interp template), so cam_wv_saturation.esm and cam_zm_evap.esm call the single law without per-document table copies: WvSaturation binds T to its T, ZMevap to its layer temperature t1; the saturation mixing ratio is then svp_to_qsat(es0, p) in both callers. The interp blend table[i] + w (table[i+1] - table[i]) differs from the Fortran (1 - w) t_i + w t_i+1 by at most 1 ulp, as before.",
   "params": [
    "T"
   ],
