     "n": 251
    }
   }
  },
  "guarded_ratio": {
   "description": "Guarded ratio of the RRTMG shortwave cloud-optics conversion (radsw.F90:437-475): ratio = x/y when y > 0, else fallback. The three solver-input ratios share the one branch structure: ssa = tau_w/tau with fallback 1 (tau = 0 -> ssa = 1), asm = tau_w_g/tau_w and fsfc = tau_w_f/tau_w with fallback 0 (tau_w = 0 -> 0). The Fortran guards the denominator with max(y, 1e-80) instead of branching, but the two are identical whenever y <= 0 selects the fallback (x/max(y,1e-80) is never evaluated in the else branch) and the max is vacuous for y > 0 (every dump ratio y > 1e-80; the stage-1 validator verifies ssa = tau_w/tau, asm = tau_w_g/tau_w, fsfc = tau_w_f/tau_w to rel 1e-12 where the denominators are positive).",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "y",
    "fallback"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": ">",
      "args": [
       "y",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "x",
       "y"
      ]
     },
     "fallback"
    ]
   }
  },
  "edge_shift": {
   "description": "The shared-edge law of the RRTMG state construction (rrtmg_state.F90:141-144, 110-120): the upper interface of RRTMG layer k is the lower interface of layer k+1, so hi(k) = lo(k+1) for k = 1..n-1 and hi(n) = the surface boundary value sfc, written as a per-k gather over the index set kset. Used for the pressure edges (pint_hi from pint_lo, with the surface pressure r_state%pintmb(num_rrtmg_levs+1) = pstate%pint(pverp), F90:158-159) and the temperature edges (T_ifc_hi from T_ifc_lo, with the surface interface temperature tint(pverp) from the surface upwelling flux, F90:110-120).",
   "params": [
    "lo",
    "sfc",
    "n",
    "kset"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "kk"
    ],
    "args": [],
    "ranges": {
     "kk": {
      "from": "kset"
     }
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "ifelse",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "<=",
       "args": [
        "kk",
        "n"
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "lo",
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          "kk",
          1
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "sfc"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "band_gather": {
   "description": "Gather of a per-band (band x lev) optics field to the McICA g-point axis: out[g, k] = x[band_of[g], k] over the g-point and level index sets named by the gset/lset template parameters (the SW and LW models bind them to their own gpt axes, ngptsw = 112 and ngptlw = 140). band_of is the fixed RRTMG k-distribution band->g-point map (rrtmg_sw_init.f90:266-280, counts 6,12,8,8,10,10,2,10,8,6,6,8,6,12; rrtmg_lw_init.f90:308, counts 10,12,16,14,16,8,12,8,12,6,8,8,4,2,2,2), declared as a [gpt]-shaped parameter in the consuming models.",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "band_of",
    "gset",
    "lset"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "g",
     "k"
    ],
    "args": [],
    "ranges": {
     "g": {
      "from": "gset"
     },
     "k": {
      "from": "lset"
     }
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "index",
     "args": [
      "x",
      {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "band_of",
        "g"
       ]
      },
      "k"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "physics_update_step": {
   "description": "The explicit state-update step of the CAM physics_update law (physics_types.F90:207-495): x_new = x + dt*tend, the single forward step applied to every state variable after each parameterization (T = T + ptend_s*dt/cpairv, F90:415-421; q = q + ptend_q*dt inside the lq gate, F90:315-317; u/v likewise), with the caller folding the ptend lq/ls flags, the win update window and the cpairv conversion into the tendency tend. Shared by cam_physics_update.esm (T_after, qraw) and the zm_convr_run -> zm_conv_evap_run state1 handoff of cam_zm.esm (t1 = t + delt dsdt, q1 = q + delt dqdt of zm_conv_intr.F90:640, with dsdt/dqdt the q1q2 tendencies).",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "tend",
    "dt"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "x",
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "tend",
       "dt"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "zero_if": {
   "description": "The threshold zeroing of the GW stress propagation (gw_common.F90:560-561: 'where (tausat <= taumin) tausat = 0' and the taudmp twin): zero_if(x, thresh, zero) = x when x > thresh, else zero. The zero is a third parameter so the fallback branch carries the units of x (the esm unit checker requires ifelse branches to share dimensions). The Fortran limits the arrays rather than the min result so that the PGI-compiled runs stay bit-reproducible; the two zeroings are the two min arguments of tau = min(taudmp, tausat) (F90:563).",
   "params": ["x", "thresh", "zero"],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {"op": "<=", "args": ["x", "thresh"]},
     "zero",
     "x"
    ]
   }
  },
  "fortran_sign": {
   "description": "The Fortran sign intrinsic as a branch (gw_common.F90:667: gwut = sign(ubtl, c - ubm)): fortran_sign(x, y, zero) = |x| when y >= zero (sign(b, a) returns |b| with the sign of a, and a = 0 counts as positive), else -|x|. The threshold zero is a third parameter so the comparison carries the units of y; the esm unit checker compares dimensioned quantities only. The Fortran sign renders the ubt/ubm sign check unnecessary for mountain waves (the comment at F90:664-666).",
   "params": ["x", "y", "zero"],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {"op": ">=", "args": ["y", "zero"]},
     {"op": "abs", "args": ["x"]},
     {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "const", "args": [], "value": -1.0, "units": "1"}, {"op": "abs", "args": ["x"]}]}
    ]
   }
  },
  "tndmax_ratio": {
   "description": "The second (ratio) tendency limiter of the GW drag (gw_common.F90:675-685): ubt_lim_ratio = tndmax/|ubt| when |ubt| > tndmax else 1, applied to both ubt and every gwut wave (F90:691-693) so the stress carried down is reduced consistently. Never binds in the orographic window (the first umcfac limiter holds |ubtl| < 4.6e-3 = tndmax at every level; the validator's ratio chain is exactly 1), but it is part of the law and is pinned structurally.",
   "params": ["x", "tndmax"],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {"op": ">", "args": [{"op": "abs", "args": ["x"]}, "tndmax"]},
     {"op": "/", "args": ["tndmax", {"op": "abs", "args": ["x"]}]},
     {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0, "units": "1"}
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}